Monstrous tanru would be resisted for reasons of malglico or malrarbau, I
suggest. Let's see you describe "kitsch" with a lujvo. Then see if I can
figure out the places, sight unseen. 

Lujvo are great for toothbrushes, but there is a whole class of word in
natural language which does not lend itself to lujvo. These words are what
give a language its soul.



